ive→9, 1&2→`lz4mid`, 3..9→`hashChain` (patternAnalysis only when nbSearches>128, i.e. level 9), 10/11→`lz4opt`, 12→`lz4opt`+fullUpdate; `favorDecSpeed` is only consulted by the opt parser. `LZ4HC_compress_generic_dictCtx` branches on `position >= 64 KB`, `position==0 && srcSize>4 KB && isStateCompatible` (mid-vs-nonmid strategy match), else `usingDictCtxHc`.\n- **lz4frame.c**: `LZ4F_compressFrame` silently overrides caller prefs — `autoFlush=1`, `stableSrc=1`, `blockSizeID` reduced by `LZ4F_optimalBSID`, `blockMode` forced to independent when `srcSize <= blockSize`, and `contentSize` auto-corrected if non-zero. Context type flips at `compressionLevel < LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN (2)`, and negative levels become `acceleration = -level+1`. `tmpBuff` size depends on `autoFlush × blockMode` (0 / 64 KB / blockSize / blockSize+128 KB). The decoder is a 15-stage state machine, so byte-at-a-time feeding is a genuinely distinct configuration; `stableDst` and `skipChecksums` are both sticky-per-frame.\n- **lz4file.c** has no compile-time config but hard-fails `readOpen` unless the first `fread` returns exactly 19 bytes, and `writeClose` skips `compressEnd` if a prior write errored.\n- **xxhash.c**: `XXH_FORCE_ALIGN_CHECK` is 0 on x86/x64, so the aligned/unaligned split is dead on this build; the live axes are `len<16`/`len&15` (32-bit) and `len<32`/`len&31` (64-bit) residue classes, seed, and the streaming `memsize` buffering boundaries.","usage":{"total_tokens":324909,"tool_uses":24,"duration_ms":1072732},"uuid":"1fcd35ff-8dd0-4888-822c-647c4a15f789","session_id":"e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62"}
