ted\n  reuse of the same state across many calls so `currentOffset` evolution / table-reset\n  thresholds (4 KB input, 0xFFFF, 1 GB) are exercised identically;\n  `LZ4_initStream` with a valid buffer, an undersized buffer, a misaligned buffer, NULL;\n  `LZ4_compress_destSize` / `LZ4_compress_destSize_extState` with targetDstSize 0, 1,\n  half of bound, and >= bound (check the `*srcSizePtr` out-param matches too);\n  `LZ4_compressBound` for 0, 1, LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE, LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE+1, negative;\n  `LZ4_versionNumber` / `LZ4_versionString` (compare the C string bytes via CStr);\n  decompression with exact / larger / smaller dstCapacity; compressedSize 0;\n  dstCapacity 0 with src==\"\\0\" srcSize==1 (expect 0) and with any other src (expect -1);\n  outputs below and far above FASTLOOP_SAFE_DISTANCE=64; blocks built to use match offsets\n  1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8..15 and >=16 (construct inputs like a repeated period-N pattern to force\n  offset N); token nibble == 15 with multi-255 extension bytes (long literal runs from\n  incompressible data, long matches from a single repeated byte over >100 KB);\n  `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial` with targetOutputSize 0, mid-literal, mid-match, and\n  > decompressed size, and with dstCapacity < targetOutputSize;\n  `LZ4_decompress_fast` with exact originalSize; the legacy `LZ4_uncompress` and\n  `LZ4_uncompress_unknownOutputSize` wrappers; in-place decompression with src placed at\n  the tail of the dst buffer.\n- FUZZ THE DECODER on malformed input: take a valid compressed block and randomly corrupt\n  bytes / truncate it, then feed the SAME corrupted bytes to both decompressors and assert\n  they return the identical value (C returns 0/-1/negative-offset values — they must match\n  exactly, not merely \"both negative\"). Do many iterations. Give both a generously sized\n  dst so neither reads out of bounds of its own buffer, and compare the produced prefix\n  bytes up to the returned length as well.\n\nIterate: run the test file with `-