8 | LZ4F_isError, LZ4F_getErrorName, LZ4F_getErrorCode | a success value, each LZ4F_ERROR_* code, and a value outside the error range | [ ] |\n193\t| 139 | LZ4F_headerSize | srcSize < 5 → frameHeader_incomplete; skippable magic → 8; plain frame → 7; +contentSize → 15; +dictID → 11; both → 19; bad magic → frameType_unknown; src=NULL → srcPtr_wrong | [ ] |\n194\t| 140 | LZ4F_getFrameInfo | fresh dctx with >= headerSize bytes (consumes header, returns BHSize hint); fewer bytes → frameHeader_incomplete with *srcSizePtr=0; dctx stopped mid-header → frameDecoding_alreadyStarted; after decoding started → cached frameInfo + next-size hint | [ ] |\n195\t| 141 | LZ4F_createDecompressionContext, LZ4F_createDecompressionContext_advanced, LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext, LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext | free returns current dStage; reset after an error then reuse for a new frame | [ ] |\n196\t| 142 | LZ4F_decompress | whole frame in one call with *dstSizePtr >= maxBlockSize → decode straight into dstBuffer | [ ] |\n197\t| 143 | LZ4F_decompress | source fed one byte at a time → dstage_storeFrameHeader / storeBlockHeader / storeCBlock / storeSuffix / storeSFrameSize all exercised | [ ] |\n198\t| 144 | LZ4F_decompress | dst capacity < maxBlockSize → decode into tmpOut then dstage_flushOut, with the flush split over several calls | [ ] |\n199\t| 145 | LZ4F_decompress | blockLinked frame → all LZ4F_updateDict branches (prefix continuation, dst history >= 64 KB, withinTmp continue, withinTmp copy-in-front, dict==tmpOutBuffer top-up, join dict+dst) | [ ] |\n200\t| 146 | LZ4F_decompress | blockIndependent frame (no dictionary management) at each blockSizeID | [ ] |\n201\t| 147 | LZ4F_decompress | decompressOptions stableDst = 1 vs 0 on a blockLinked frame (end-of-call history preservation skipped vs performed) | [ ] |\n202\t| 148 | LZ4F_decompress | decompressOptions skipChecksums = 1 on a frame carrying content and block checksums (sticky for the rest of the frame) | [ ] |\n203\t| 149 | LZ4F_decompress | corrupted content checksum → contentChecksum_invalid; corrupted block checksum on a compressed block and on a stored block → blockChecksum_invalid; corrupted header checksum → headerChecksum_invalid | [ ] |\n204\t| 150 | LZ4F_decompress | bad magic → frameType_unknown; FLG version != 1 → headerVersion_wrong; FLG bit1 / BD bit7 / BD low nibble set → reservedFlag_set; blockSizeID < 4 → maxBlockSize_invalid | [ ] |\n205\t| 151 | LZ4F_decompress | stored (uncompressed) blocks → dstage_copyDirect, including a copy split across calls and the following block checksum | [ ] |\n206\t| 152 | LZ4F_decompress | declared block size > frame maxBlockSize → maxBlockSize_invalid; blockHeader == 0 → clean end of frame; truncated compressed block → decompressionFailed | [ ] |\n207\t| 153 | LZ4F_decompress | contentSize present in the header but decoded total differs → frameSize_wrong at dstage_getSuffix | [ ] |\n208\t| 154 | LZ4F_decompress | skippable frame (magic LZ4F_MAGIC_SKIPPABLE_START..+0xF): content size 0, small, larger than the supplied input (split over calls), and 8-byte header split across calls | [ ] |\n209\t| 155 | LZ4F_decompress | two frames concatenated in one dctx (auto reset at end of frame); frame followed by a skippable frame; srcSize=0 → returns minFHSize hint; dstBuffer NULL with *dstSizePtr=0 (hint-only call) | [ ] |\n210\t| 156 | LZ4F_decompress_usingDict | dict supplied before init (dStage <= dstage_init) → applied; supplied mid-frame → ignored; dictSize > 1 GB → truncated to the last 64 KB | [ ] |\n211\t\n212\t## lz4file\n213\t\n214\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n215\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n216\t| 157 | LZ4F_writeOpen | prefsPtr = NULL → maxWriteSize 64 KB; blockSizeID default/max64KB/max256KB/max1MB/max4MB; invalid blockSizeID → maxBlockSize_invalid; fp = NULL or handle = NULL → parameter_null | [ ] |\n217\t| 158 | LZ4F_write | size = 0; size < maxWriteSize; size == maxWriteSize; size > maxWriteSize (chunking loop); buf = NULL or handle = NULL → parameter_null | [ ] |\n218\t| 159 | LZ4F_writeOpen + LZ4F_write | non-default prefs forwarded to compressBegin/compressUpdate: contentChecksum, blockChecksum, contentSize, dictID, level 0/9/12, autoFlush 0/1, blockLinked vs blockIndependent | [ ] |\n219\t| 160 | LZ4F_writeClose | normal close (compressEnd + fwrite); after a previous write error (errCode set → compressEnd skipped); handle = NULL → parameter_null | [ ] |\n220\t| 161 | LZ4F_readOpen | file shorter than LZ4F_HEADER_SIZE_MAX (19) → io_read; frame blockSizeID → srcBufMaxSize 64 KB / 256 KB / 1 MB / 4 MB; invalid blockSizeID → maxBlockSize_invalid; fp/handle NULL → parameter_null | [ ] |\n221\t| 162 | LZ4F_read, LZ4F_readClose | size = 0; size < remaining frame content; size > frame content (EOF break → short count); several sequential reads; frames with linked vs independent blocks and with checksums; handle/buf NULL → parameter_null | [ ] |\n222\t\n223\t## xxhash (namespaced LZ4_XXH*)\n224\t\n225\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n226\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n227\t| 163 | LZ4_XXH32 | length 0 with a valid pointer and with NULL; seed 0 and seed 0x9E3779B1 | [ ] |\n228\t| 164 | LZ4_XXH32 | length 1, 2, 3 (PROCESS1 chain only) and 4, 5, 6, 7 (PROCESS4 + 0..3 PROCESS1) | [ ] |\n229\t| 165 | LZ4_XXH32 | length 8..15 — every remaining `len & 15` residue class — with seed 0 and non-zero | [ ] |\n230\t| 166 | LZ4_XXH32 | length 16 (first full stripe), 17, 31, 32, 100, 1 MB; seed 0 and non-zero; 4-byte-aligned and deliberately misaligned input pointers | [ ] |\n231\t| 167 | LZ4_XXH32_createState, LZ4_XXH32_freeState, LZ4_XXH32_reset, LZ4_XXH32_update, LZ4_XXH32_digest | single update equal to the one-shot result; seed 0 and non-zero; freeState(NULL) | [ ] |\n232\t| 168 | LZ4_XXH32_update | 1 byte at a time; chunks summing to < 16 (pure mem32 buffering, large_len unset); chunks crossing the 16-byte stripe boundary with an unaligned leftover; total >= 16 reached only via small chunks (large_len via total_len_32) | [ ] |\n233\t| 169 | LZ4_XXH32_digest, LZ4_XXH32_copyState | digest called twice; digest then further updates then digest again; copyState then diverging updates on the copy | [ ] |\n234\t| 170 | LZ4_XXH32_canonicalFromHash, LZ4_XXH32_hashFromCanonical | round-trip of 0, 0xFFFFFFFF and an arbitrary hash (big-endian canonical byte order) | [ ] |\n235\t| 171 | LZ4_XXH64 | length 0 (valid pointer and NULL), 1..7, 8, 9..31 (every `len & 31` residue class), 32, 33, 63, 64, 1 MB; seed 0 and non-zero; 8-byte-aligned vs misaligned input | [ ] |\n236\t| 172 | LZ4_XXH64_createState, LZ4_XXH64_freeState, LZ4_XXH64_reset, LZ4_XXH64_update, LZ4_XXH64_digest, LZ4_XXH64_copyState | single update equal to the one-shot; 1-byte chunks; chunks summing < 32 (mem64 buffering); chunks straddling the 32-byte stripe boundary; total_len < 32 vs >= 32 at digest time | [ ] |\n237\t| 173 | LZ4_XXH64_canonicalFromHash, LZ4_XXH64_hashFromCanonical, LZ4_XXH_versionNumber | round-trip of 0, UINT64_MAX and an arbitrary hash; version constant | [ ] |\n238\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_017SZTSCokiHMF65SBLwxB1T","session_id":"e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62","uuid":"c58cc420-0689-46a6-9b79-a48e7ab5896a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T05:33:37.095Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write lz4 block differential tests"}
