treamDecode, LZ4_setStreamDecode | create/free/free(NULL); dictionary NULL with size 0 (reset), small dict, exactly 64 KB dict | [ ] |\n| 54 | LZ4_decompress_safe_continue | very first block, prefixSize==0 → plain safe decode | [ ] |\n| 55 | LZ4_decompress_safe_continue | contiguous dst (prefixEnd==dest), prefixSize < 64KB-1, extDictSize==0 → withSmallPrefix | [ ] |\n| 56 | LZ4_decompress_safe_continue | contiguous dst, prefixSize >= 64KB-1 → withPrefix64k | [ ] |\n| 57 | LZ4_decompress_safe_continue | contiguous dst with an externalDict already recorded → doubleDict | [ ] |\n| 58 | LZ4_decompress_safe_continue | dst switches buffer or ring wraps → prefix becomes extDict (forceExtDict) | [ ] |\n| 59 | LZ4_decompress_safe_continue | ring buffer sized exactly LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize(maxBlockSize) = 65536+14+maxBlockSize | [ ] |\n| 60 | LZ4_decompress_safe_continue | synchronized small ring buffer (< 64 KB) with exact per-block decompressed sizes | [ ] |\n| 61 | LZ4_decompress_safe_continue | mid-stream failure (dstCapacity too small / corrupt block) → negative, prefix state untouched | [ ] |\n| 62 | LZ4_decompress_fast_continue | first block; prefix continuation; prefix→extDict switch (all three branches) | [ ] |\n| 63 | LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize | maxBlockSize 0, 16, 64 KB, 4 MB; negative → 0; > LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE → 0 | [ ] |\n| 64 | LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict, LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_usingDict | dictSize=0; dictStart+dictSize==dst with dictSize>=64KB-1; same with small dictSize; separate ext dict with a match straddling the dict/block boundary | [ ] |\n| 65 | LZ4_decompress_fast_usingDict, LZ4_decompress_safe_forceExtDict, LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_forceExtDict, LZ4_decompress_safe_withPrefix64k, LZ4_decompress_fast_withPrefix64k | dictSize < 64 KB (checkOffset enabled) vs >= 64 KB (disabled); legacy 64 KB-prefix decoders | [ ] |\n\n## lz4hc block\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 66 | LZ4_compress_HC | compressionLevel = 0 and negative → coerced to LZ4HC_CLEVEL_DEFAULT (9) | [ ] |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0189HqSEkrEA5n2sEQAkrBNS","session_id":"e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62","uuid":"5836ae92-04ee-4858-a7fb-c3ae070a6166","timestamp":"2026-08-31T05:34:39.665Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write lz4hc differential tests"}
