 `c_src/src/xxhash.c`, `c_src/include/xxhash.h`,\n`c_src/src/lz4file.c`, `c_src/include/lz4file.h`.\n\nHARD RULES\n- NEVER modify anything in `c_src/`.\n- Do NOT modify `translation/src/*.rs`. You write TESTS ONLY. Report any genuine C-vs-Rust\n  divergence precisely (function, exact inputs, C result, Rust result), leaving the test\n  failing.\n- Never call Rust functions directly — every call goes through a `.so` symbol via libloading.\n- CRITICAL: opaque state (`LZ4_XXH32_state_t`, `LZ4_XXH64_state_t`, `LZ4_readFile_t`,\n  `LZ4_writeFile_t`) must be created by EACH library for ITSELF via that library's own\n  `LZ4_XXH32_createState` / `LZ4F_readOpen` / `LZ4F_writeOpen`, and freed/closed by the\n  same library. NEVER hand a context from one library to the other. `LZ4_XXH32_copyState`\n  must only copy between two states from the SAME library.\n- Cargo has NO network access. ALWAYS pass `--offline`, e.g.\n  `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test xxhash 2>&1 | tail -40`\n\nHARNESS (already written, read it: `translation/tests/common/mod.rs`)\nStart each file with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::os::raw::{c_char, c_int, c_uint, c_void};\n```\n`libs()` -> `&'static Pair`; `l.sym::<FnType>(\"name\")` -> `(c_fn, rust_fn)`.\nHelpers: `Rng::new(seed)`, `gen(&mut rng, Shape::X, len)`, `ALL_SHAPES`,\n`interesting_sizes()`, `same_usize_and_bytes`, `same_int_and_bytes`, `same_full_buffers`,\n`err(code)` = `(size_t)-code`, `is_err_range(r)`, the `LZ4F_preferences_t` /\n`LZ4F_frameInfo_t` / `LZ4F_compressOptions_t` / `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t` `#[repr(C)]`\nmirrors and the `LZ4F_*` constants. Define extra `type Fn... = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(...)`\naliases locally.\n\nxxhash.rs REQUIREMENTS\n- One `#[test] fn row_NN_...()` per CONFIGS row 163..173; every number must appear in a\n  test function name. Plus error-path tests for the xxhash ERRORS.md rows.\n- Exhaustively sweep length 0..=300 for BOTH `LZ4_XXH32` and `LZ4_XXH64` (covers