{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a34922b590159a8a1","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_017SZTSCokiHMF65SBLwxB1T","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-glo4ZM/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-iXd6IA/e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62/tasks/a34922b590159a8a1.output","summary":"Done. Wrote exactly one new file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iXd6IA/translation/tests/lz4_block.rs` (2468 lines). Nothing in `c_src/` or `translation/src/` was touched.\n\n## Result\n\n```\n34 tests, 34 passed, 0 failed — 20.2 s wall\ncd translation && cargo test --offline --release --test lz4_block\n```\n\nOne `#[test] fn row_NN_…` per CONFIGS row, `row_01` … `row_34`, each property-style with a fixed seed (`Rng::new(row_number)`) looping over many sizes × all 5 `Shape`s.\n\n**No genuine C-vs-Rust behavioural divergences were found in rows 1–34.** Every return value, every destination byte, every `*srcSizePtr` out-param and every 16416-byte `LZ4_stream_t` state image matched exactly.\n\n## How it's checked\n- C and Rust each get their own `0xCD`-filled dst with a 64-byte trailing guard; `same_int_and_bytes` + `same_full_buffers` on the *whole* allocation (catches divergent scribbles past the reported length).\n- Every compression test cross-decompresses: C output through the **Rust** decoder and Rust output through the **C** decoder, both must recover the original.\n- `LZ4_compress_fast_extState` / `_extState_fastReset` / `_destSize_extState` use one caller-allocated, 8-byte-aligned `LZ4_sizeofState()` (= 16416) buffer **per library**, and the full state image is compared after every call — so `currentOffset`, `tableType`, `dictSize` and the whole 4096-entry hash table are diffed too.\n- A hand-rolled `Blk` block builder gives exact control of token nibbles, multi-255 extension chains and match offsets; a `build_block` generator produces random well-formed blocks.\n\n## Coverage highlights\nsrcSize 0/1/12/13 and NULL src; 65546/65547/65548 byU16→byU32 pivot; 256 KB/1 MB/4 MB; 100 KB single-byte run (4×255 ML chain); accel `i32::MIN,-1000,-1,0,1,2,3,8,64,65536,65537,65538,1000000,i32::MAX` (plus assertions that `<1` behaves as 1 and `>MAX` clamps to MAX); `LZ4_initStream` valid/undersized/misaligned(off 1..7, C returns NULL)/NULL; `destSize` targets 0/1/half-bound/≥bound with `*srcSizePtr` verified; `compressBound(0,1,MAX,MAX+1,negative)` + 1000-value sweep; `versionString` compared via `CStr`; offsets 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8..15,≥16 both hand-built and forced via period-N inputs; outputs 5..140 bytes and ≫64; tails of exactly 5..11 bytes (the `oend-MATCH_SAFEGUARD_DISTANCE` slow copy); partial decode target 0/mid-literal/mid-match/oversized/`dstCapacity<target`; in-place decode with src at the tail of dst using `LZ4_DECOMPRESS_INPLACE_MARGIN`; `LZ4_uncompress` and `LZ4_uncompress_unknownOutputSize` asserted identical to `decompress_fast`/`decompress_safe`.\n\n**Fuzzer (row 29):** 2,000,000 corruption iterations (byte flips, bit flips, truncation, garbage, appended junk, zeroed runs → offset-0 matches) fed identically to both decoders. Measured return distribution: **777,503 positive, 349 zero, 9,602 `-1`, 1,212,546 other negative `-(ip-src)-1` offsets** — all exact matches, not just \"both negative\". Plus 60,000 hand-built rule violations (short last-literals, out-of-range offsets, truncated 255-extension chains).\n\n## Two notes (not divergences)\n1. **`LZ4_prepareTable`'s `currentOffset > 1 GB` (byU32) reset is unreachable through `LZ4_compress_fast_extState_fastReset`** — byU32 is only selected when `srcSize >= LZ4_64Klimit`, which is also `>= 4 KB`, so the `inputSize >= 4 KB` arm always resets `currentOffset` to 0 first. Documented in a comment in `row_16`; that arm needs the streaming API (CONFIGS rows 35+). The byU16 `currentOffset + srcSize >= 0xFFFF` threshold *is* crossed repeatedly (2400 chained calls), as are the 4 KB and `tableType`-mismatch resets.\n2. While running the full suite I noticed a **different** test target, `translation/tests/lz4hc.rs` (not mine, appeared during my session), aborts with SIGSEGV. `--test lz4_block` and `--test smoke` are unaffected.","usage":{"total_tokens":188970,"tool_uses":54,"duration_ms":1271831},"uuid":"7ef31c85-ca52-4135-a402-8a15cceac449","session_id":"e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62"}
