e` are unaffected."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a34922b590159a8a1 (use SendMessage with to: 'a34922b590159a8a1', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 190099\ntool_uses: 54\nduration_ms: 1271832</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62","uuid":"8314c0d5-df69-4681-94c4-68d8f99b88f8","timestamp":"2026-08-31T05:54:45.101Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iXd6IA\n\nTASK: write ONE new file `translation/tests/lz4_block.rs` containing differential tests\ncovering rows 1-34 of `translation/CONFIGS.md` (sections \"lz4 block — one-shot compression\"\nand \"lz4 block — decompression\"). Read those rows first, plus the relevant parts of\n`c_src/src/lz4.c` and `c_src/include/lz4.h`.\n\nHARD RULES\n- NEVER modify anything in `c_src/`.\n- Do NOT modify `translation/src/*.rs`. You write TESTS ONLY. If you find a behavioural\n  divergence between C and Rust, leave the test in place (failing) and REPORT it precisely\n  in your final message: function name, exact inputs, C result, Rust result.\n- Never call Rust functions directly. Every call must go through a `.so` symbol looked up\n  with libloading. The harness already does this.\n- Cargo has NO network access. ALWAYS pass `--offline`:\n  `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test lz4_block 2>&1 | tail -40`\n\nHARNESS (already written, read it: `translation/tests/common/mod.rs`)\nStart your file with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::os::raw::{c_char, c_int, c_void};\n```\n`libs()` returns a `&'static Pair`. Use `l.sym::<FnType>(\"Symbol_name\")` which returns\n`(c_fn, rust_fn)` — a tuple of the SAME symbol from the C .so and the Rust .so.\nAvailable helpers: `Rng::new(seed)` (deterministic xorshift; `.below(n)`, `.range(lo,hi)`,\n`.byte()`, `.next_u32()`), shape generators `gen(&mut rng, Shape::X, len)` with\n`ALL_SHAP