{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a18d3387b61465dcc","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0189HqSEkrEA5n2sEQAkrBNS","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-glo4ZM/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-iXd6IA/e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62/tasks/a18d3387b61465dcc.output","summary":"All done. Final state: **38 tests, 38 pass, 0 fail.**\n\n## What was written\n\nSingle new file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iXd6IA/translation/tests/lz4hc.rs` (~2470 lines), one `#[test] fn row_NN_…` per `CONFIGS.md` row 66-103. Nothing else was touched (`c_src/` and `translation/src/*.rs` timestamps unchanged).\n\nRuntime: **18.9 s** wall with default parallelism, **82 s** with `--test-threads=1` (well under the 400 s budget).\n\nEvery test is property-style (fixed seed `Rng::new(row)`), loops over `ALL_SHAPES` × many sizes × repetitions, gives C and Rust **separate `0xCD`-filled destination buffers with a 32-byte guard tail**, compares return value + whole buffer (`same_int_and_bytes` + `same_full_buffers`), and cross-decompresses (C's HC output through Rust's `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict` and vice-versa). All opaque HC state is created/initialised/freed by the owning library only.\n\n## Genuine C-vs-Rust divergences\n\n**None.** No test is left failing.\n\n## Notable findings (shared behaviour, not divergences) that shaped the tests\n\n1. **`Vec::new().as_ptr()` == `0x1`.** With `srcSize == 0` and that dangling pointer, the level ≥ 10 optimal parser computes `mflimit = iend - MFLIMIT`, which wraps to a huge unsigned address, so `ip <= mflimit` is true and both libraries read address `0x1` and segfault **identically**. Fixed in the test by shadowing `gen`/`gen_incompressible` with wrappers that force a real allocation. (Levels 1-9 are unaffected because they check `*srcSizePtr < LZ4_minLength` first.)\n2. **The C reference is built without `NDEBUG`** (`CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` is empty in `c_src/build/CMakeCache.txt`), so its `assert()`s are live while Rust has no equivalents. Three places had to be avoided:\n   - `LZ4_compressHC2_continue` hard-wires `dstCapacity = 0` with `notLimited`, which trips `assert(op <= oend)` in `LZ4MID_compress` (`c_src/src/lz4hc.c:743`). It is therefore driven at cLevel 0/3/9/12 (0 → 9); levels 1/2 are covered through `LZ4_compressHC2_limitedOutput_continue` with a real capacity.\n   - `LZ4_saveDictHC` has `if (safeBuffer == NULL) assert(dictSize == 0)` (`lz4hc.c:1751`), so the `safeBuffer = NULL` case is only exercised with `maxDictSize < 4` (clamped to 0).\n   - `LZ4_slideInputBufferHC` leaves `prefixStart == NULL`, and the deprecated `LZ4_compressHC2*_continue` wrappers do no auto-init, so calling them straight after a slide dereferences near-NULL in *both* libraries; the test re-arms the context with `LZ4_resetStreamStateHC` (asserting exactly `0` on success / `1` on failure, per the inverted convention).\n3. **\"Undersized state\" is not reachable through the state-taking entry points**: `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC`, `_fastReset`, `LZ4_compress_HC_destSize` and `LZ4_resetStreamStateHC` all hard-code `sizeof(LZ4_streamHC_t)`. Row 81/85 therefore cover it via `LZ4_initStreamHC(buf, size)` returning `NULL` for `size ∈ {0,1,7,8,1024,sizeof-1}` in both libraries; the *misaligned* case is driven directly through `extStateHC` / `_fastReset` / `withStateHC` (all return 0) and `initStreamHC`/`resetStreamStateHC` (NULL / 1). `LZ4_sizeofStateHC` and `LZ4_sizeofStreamStateHC` agree (262200) in both.\n4. **`LZ4HC_searchExtDict` was driven directly** with its exact exported signature (`(ip, ipIndex, iLowLimit, iHighLimit, dictCtx, gDictEndIndex, currentBestML, nbAttempts) -> LZ4HC_match_t{off,len,back}` returned by value), each library against **its own** `LZ4_loadDictHC`-prepared context, over 5 dict sizes × 5 dict levels × 5 `gDictEndIndex` shifts × `nbAttempts` 1/2 × `currentBestML` 0/3 × ~230 `ip` positions × 2 `iLowLimit` choices. The dictionary is embedded 64 KB into a larger allocation so a chain step below the dictionary start still reads mapped, identical memory. Non-vacuity is asserted (`> 100` real matches found and at least one non-zero `back`). It is *also* exercised indirectly via `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary` with a level-9/12 dict and a level-1/2 working stream (`LZ4MID_searchHCDict`).\n5. **Row 96 (2 GB re-anchor)** is reached cheaply: `ctx->end += srcSize` happens *before* compression, so 70 rounds of a deliberately failing 64 MB block (`dstCapacity = 0`, incompressible data → the `ip += 1 + ((ip-anchor)>>9)` skip walks it in ~6 k steps) grow `dictLimit` by 64 MB per round via `LZ4HC_setExternalDict`, crossing the 2 GB threshold at round 32 without ever compressing 2 GB. The post-re-anchor state is additionally compared through `LZ4_saveDictHC`.\n6. `LZ4_favorDecompressionSpeed` is verified to *actually matter*: the test asserts that at least one level-10/12 case produces different output for `favor=1` vs `favor=0`, and that it is a no-op at levels 2/9.\n\nCross-configuration invariants are also asserted in both libraries (levels −1000/−1/0 byte-identical to 9; 13/100/1000/`INT_MAX` byte-identical to 12; a fresh `LZ4_createStreamHC` stream identical to one-shot level 9; `extStateHC` identical to `LZ4_compress_HC`; `LZ4_compressHC` identical to level 9; a dirty `LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast` identical to a fresh stream; `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary(NULL)` identical to a plain stream).","usage":{"total_tokens":245869,"tool_uses":92,"duration_ms":2124280},"uuid":"72b88379-d450-4c4d-9b72-5f25c040186e","session_id":"e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62"}
