se rows first, plus\nthe relevant parts of `c_src/src/lz4.c` and `c_src/include/lz4.h`.\n\nHARD RULES\n- NEVER modify anything in `c_src/`.\n- Do NOT modify `translation/src/*.rs`. You write TESTS ONLY. If you find a behavioural\n  divergence between C and Rust, leave the test in place (failing) and REPORT it precisely\n  in your final message: function name, exact inputs, C result, Rust result.\n- Never call Rust functions directly. Every call goes through a `.so` symbol via libloading.\n- CRITICAL: opaque state (LZ4_stream_t, LZ4_streamDecode_t) must be created by EACH library\n  for ITSELF via that library's own `LZ4_createStream`/`LZ4_createStreamDecode`, and freed\n  by the same library. NEVER pass a C-allocated context to the Rust .so or vice versa —\n  internal layouts are independent. Same rule for caller-allocated `LZ4_sizeofState()` /\n  `LZ4_sizeofStreamState()` buffers: allocate one buffer per library.\n- Cargo has NO network access. ALWAYS pass `--offline`:\n  `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test lz4_stream 2>&1 | tail -40`\n\nHARNESS (already written, read it: `translation/tests/common/mod.rs`)\nStart your file with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::os::raw::{c_char, c_int, c_void};\n```\n`libs()` -> `&'static Pair`; `l.sym::<FnType>(\"name\")` -> `(c_fn, rust_fn)`.\nHelpers: `Rng::new(seed)` (`.below`, `.range`, `.byte`), `gen(&mut rng, Shape::X, len)`,\n`ALL_SHAPES`, `interesting_sizes()`, `same_int_and_bytes`, `same_full_buffers`,\n`first_diff`, `hexdump`. Signature aliases: `FnCompressDefault`, `FnCompressFast`,\n`FnCompressBound`, `FnDecompressSafe`, `FnDecompressSafePartial`, `FnDecompressFast`,\n`FnVoidToInt`, `FnVoidToPtr`, `FnFreePtr`, `FnPtrToInt`. Add local `type Fn... =\nunsafe extern \"C\" fn(...)` aliases as needed.\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n- One `#[test] fn row_NN_...()` per CONFIGS row 35..65; every row number must appear in\n  some test function name so coverage is auditable.\n- PROPERTY-STYLE: loop over MANY randomized multi-block sequences per test (fixed seed,\n  e.g. `Rng::new(row_number)`), varying block count (1..30), per-block sizes (including 0,\n  tiny, ~4 KB threshold, ~64 KB, >64 KB) and `Shape`s. Keep the whole file under ~150s.\n- Drive C and Rust in LOCKSTEP: for each step, run the C call and the Rust call on\n  identical inputs with their own separate output buffers pre-filled with a 0xCD sentinel,\n  then compare return value and bytes. A streaming bug usually shows up several blocks in,\n  so the whole chained sequence must be compared step by step, not just the final output.\n- Also cross-decompress: decode the C-produced block chain with the Rust streaming decoder\n  and vice versa, verifying the original data is recovered in both directions.\n- Cover explicitly, per the CONFIGS rows:\n  * `LZ4_createStream`/`LZ4_freeStream`/`LZ4_freeStream(NULL)`/deprecated `LZ4_resetStream`;\n    a caller-provided zeroed buffer used as a stream then `LZ4_compress_fast_continue`.\n  * `LZ4_resetStream_fast` reuse of a stream that already compressed data.\n  * `LZ4_loadDict` with dictSize 0, 3 (<HASH_UNIT=8), 8, 32 KB, 65536 exactly, 100 KB\n    (check the returned value too); `LZ4_loadDictSlow` with the same sizes.\n  * `LZ4_compress_fast_continue`: contiguous-prefix continuation (src == previous dictEnd),\n    with dictSize <64 KB and >=64 KB; separate-buffer src after loadDict (extDict);\n    an alternating double buffer; a ring buffer smaller than 64 KB where src overlaps the\n    dictionary; a previous dictSize < 4; dstCapacity < LZ4_compressBound(srcSize) (expect 0\n    and identical stream invalidation behaviour afterwards — keep driving both streams and\n    compare); acceleration 0/1/64/1000000 on chained blocks; a long run of blocks with a\n    large cumulative size to approach the renorm path (cap total work so the test stays\n    fast — a few hundred MB of cumulative offset is too slow, so instead just verify the\n    behaviour is identical over as much as you can afford, e.g. a few hundred blocks).\n  * `LZ4_attach_dictionary` with a dictionary stream (each library gets its own dict\n    stream), srcSize <=4 KB and >4 KB; dictionaryStream = NULL; a dictCtx with dictSize 0.\n  * `LZ4_saveDict` with maxDictSize 64 KB, smaller than current dictSize, 0;\n    `LZ4_compress_forceExtDict`.\n  * Legacy/deprecated: `LZ4_compress`, `LZ4_compress_limitedOutput`, `LZ4_compress_withState`,\n    `LZ4_compress_limitedOutput_withState`, `LZ4_compress_continue`,\n    `LZ4_compress_limitedOutput_continue`, `LZ4_create`, `LZ4_slideInputBuffer`,\n    `LZ4_resetStreamState`, `LZ4_sizeofStreamState`.\n  * Decode side: `LZ4_createStreamDecode`/`LZ4_freeStreamDecode`/free(NULL);\n    `LZ4_setStreamDecode` with NULL+0, a small dict, exactly 64 KB;\n    `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue` for first block, contiguous dst with prefix <64KB-1 and\n    >=64KB-1, contiguous dst with an existing extDict (doubleDict), a dst buffer switch,\n    a ring buffer sized exactly `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize(maxBlockSize)`, a small\n    synchronized ring buffer, and a mid-stream failure (too-small dstCapacity / corrupt\n    block) after which you keep using both decoders and compare;\n    `LZ4_decompress_fast_continue` on all three branches;\n    `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize` for 0, 16, 65536, 4 MB, negative, > LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE;\n    `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_usingDict`,\n    `LZ4_decompress_fast_usingDict`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_forceExtDict`,\n    `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_forceExtDict`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_withPrefix64k`,\n    `LZ4_decompress_fast_withPrefix64k` — with dictSize 0, <64 KB, ==64 KB, >64 KB, a\n    dictionary contiguous with dst, and a match straddling the dict/block boundary.\n- FUZZ: corrupt/truncate blocks in a chain and assert C and Rust return the identical value\n  at the identical step (exact values, not just \"both failed\").\n\nIterate: run with `--offline --release`; fix YOUR TEST when the test itself is wrong.\nOnly genuine C-vs-Rust behavioural differences should remain failing.\n\nFinish by reporting: test count, pass/fail counts, and a precise list of any genuine\nC-vs-Rust divergences.","agentId":"a3448a90c8ffceca8","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"2ae8d6193acf9ee0","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iXd6IA/translation/tests/lz4_stream.rs` — 3705 lines, one new file. Nothing under `c_src/` or `translation/src/` was touched (verified with `find -newermt`).\n\n## Results\n\n- **32 tests, 32 pass, 0 fail.**\n- Runtime: **6.7 s** wall (parallel), **78 s** single-threaded — both well inside the 150 s budget.\n- Full crate suite still green (`lz4_block.rs` 34 pass, `lz4file.rs`, `smoke.rs`).\n- Coverage audit: `row_35_…` … `row_65_…` all present (one test per CONFIGS row 35-65), plus `fuzz_rows_54_62_corrupted_and_truncated_chains`.\n\n## Genuine C-vs-Rust divergences found\n\n**None.** Every C/Rust pair agreed on return value, payload bytes, and full destination-buffer contents (including scratch bytes written past the reported output but inside `dstCapacity`) across every configuration exercised.\n\n## Notes on the approach\n\n- Each library creates/frees its own `LZ4_stream_t`/`LZ4_streamDecode_t` and its own `LZ4_sizeofStreamState()` caller buffers; no opaque state ever crosses libraries. Input buffers are shared (identical pointers), destination buffers are separate and pre-filled with `0xCD` plus a 64-byte guard that is asserted intact.\n- Cross-decompression is wired in structurally: the C-produced block chain is always fed to the *Rust* decoder and vice versa.\n- `LZ4_renormDictT` (row 49) is reached *for real*, not approximated: `LZ4_loadDict(stream, dict, 3)` returns early leaving `tableType == clearedTable` and `currentOffset == 64 KB`, so ~32 766 cheap `LZ4_resetStream_fast` calls walk `currentOffset` to