rDecSpeed 0 and 1 at levels 0/1/10/12; srcSize 0/1/blockSize-1/blockSize/\n    blockSize+1/N*blockSize; incompressible data (stored-block path); dstCapacity one byte\n    below `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` (expect `err(11)` dstMaxSize_tooSmall).\n  * `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` and `LZ4F_compressBound` with prefs NULL, autoFlush 0 and 1,\n    srcSize 0, and each blockSizeID.\n  * `LZ4F_createCDict` / `LZ4F_createCDict_advanced` / `LZ4F_freeCDict` / `freeCDict(NULL)`\n    with dictSize 0, small, just under 64 KB, exactly 64 KB, > 64 KB; and a custom\n    `LZ4F_CustomMem` (its struct is `{ LZ4F_AllocFunction customAlloc; LZ4F_CallocFunction\n    customCalloc; LZ4F_FreeFunction customFree; void* opaqueState; }` — check lz4frame.h;\n    supply `extern \"C\"` shims over libc malloc/calloc/free, including the documented\n    \"calloc may be NULL\" variant).\n  * `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` at level 0/1 and level >= 2, cdict NULL and non-NULL,\n    blockIndependent multi-block vs blockLinked.\n  * `LZ4F_createCompressionContext(_advanced)` / `LZ4F_freeCompressionContext` /\n    `freeCompressionContext(NULL)`; version = LZ4F_VERSION.\n  * The LOW-LEVEL pipeline driven directly and step by step:\n    `LZ4F_compressBegin` (dstCapacity < 19 → `err(11)`, exactly 19, prefs NULL vs fully\n    populated) then a sequence of `LZ4F_compressUpdate` calls then `LZ4F_flush` then\n    `LZ4F_compressEnd`, with: autoFlush 1 and 0; stableSrc 1 and 0; blockLinked and\n    blockIndependent; many randomized update-size sequences (including 0-sized updates,\n    sub-blockSize updates that accumulate in tmpIn, and updates crossing blockSize);\n    dstCapacity exactly `LZ4F_compressBound(srcSize, prefs)` and one byte less;\n    `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` alone and INTERLEAVED with `LZ4F_compressUpdate` (the\n    COMPRESSED↔UNCOMPRESSED switch forces an implicit flush — verify byte-identical output);\n    `LZ4F_flush` with nothing buffered (expect 0) and with a partial block buffered;\n    `LZ4F_compressEnd` with a declared contentSize that does not match the total fed\n    (expect `err(14)` frameSize_wrong) and with dstCapacity < 4 / < 8-with-content-checksum\n    (expect `err(11)`); `LZ4F_compressUpdate`/`flush`/`compressEnd` called BEFORE\n    `LZ4F_compressBegin` and AFTER a completed `LZ4F_compressEnd` (expect `err(20)`\n    compressionState_uninitialized).\n  * cctx REUSE: a second and third frame on the same cctx where the compressionLevel crosses\n    `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN` (2) in both directions and the blockSizeID grows (context/tmpBuff\n    realloc paths). Assert frames are byte-identical to the same frame produced on a fresh\n    cctx in both libraries.\n  * `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict`, `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDictOnce`,\n    `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict` with dictSize < 64 KB and > 64 KB, level < 2 and >= 2,\n    blockLinked and blockIndependent, prefs NULL vs prefs carrying a dictID.\n  * `LZ4F_getBlockSize` for blockSizeID 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8 and some out-of-range values\n    (e.g. 100, u32::MAX) — assert the exact value including `err(2)` for invalid IDs.\n  * `LZ4F_getVersion`, `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max`.\n  * `LZ4F_isError` / `LZ4F_getErrorName` / `LZ4F_getErrorCode` for 0, every value\n    `err(1)..=err(24)`, and values outside the error range (e.g. 0, 1, 1000, `err(25)`,\n    `err(100)`, `usize::MAX/2`). Compare `LZ4F_getErrorName`'s returned C STRING bytes via\n    `CStr`, not just the pointer.\n  * `LZ4F_headerSize` with srcSize < 5, a skippable magic (→8), a plain frame (→7),\n    +contentSize (→15), +dictID (→11), both (→19), a bad magic (→`err(13)`), src = NULL\n    (→`err(15)`).\n  * `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` on a fresh dctx with >= headerSize bytes, with fewer bytes\n    (→`err(12)`, and `*srcSizePtr` must be set to 0 — compare that out-param), on a dctx\n    stopped mid-header (→`err(19)` frameDecoding_alreadyStarted), and after decoding has\n    started (cached frameInfo + next-size hint). Compare the whole returned\n    `LZ4F_frameInfo_t` struct field by field AND the returned hint.\n  * `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext(_advanced)`, `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext` (which\n    returns the current `dStage` — assert the exact value for a fresh ctx, a mid-frame ctx\n    and a completed ctx), `LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext` (reset after an error then reuse\n    for a new frame).\n\nIterate: run with `--offline --release`; fix YOUR TEST when the test itself is at fault\n(wrong signature, wrong buffer size, wrong expectation about C behaviour — the C is always\nright). Only genuine C-vs-Rust behavioural differences should remain failing.\n\nFinish by reporting: test count, pass/fail counts, runtime, and a precise list of any\ngenuine C-vs-Rust divergences."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01TL2naY2UAoAtNZDcd2C14J","session_id":"e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62","uuid":"62b0631b-e6f9-4eee-8a09-57021144cbd3","timestamp":"2026-08-31T06:17:19.315Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write lz4frame compression tests"}
