unsafe extern \"C\" fn(...)` aliases as needed.\n\nKEY TECHNIQUE\nBuild reference frames with the C library's `LZ4F_compressFrame` (or the low-level pipeline)\nso both decoders receive EXACTLY the same input bytes. For the malformed cases, hand-craft\nor surgically corrupt the frame bytes. For every `LZ4F_decompress` call, C and Rust get\ntheir OWN dst buffers (0xCD-filled, with a guard tail) and their own `dstSize`/`srcSize`\nin/out variables — compare the return value (the \"hint\"), BOTH out-params\n(`*dstSizePtr`, `*srcSizePtr`) and the produced bytes after EVERY call.\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n- One `#[test] fn row_NNN_...()` per CONFIGS row 142..156 (every number must appear in a\n  test function name) plus `#[test] fn err_NN_...()` tests for ERRORS.md rows 24..55 (every\n  number 24..=55 must appear in some test function name; for the rows that ERRORS.md marks\n  as UNREACHABLE or as allocation failures that cannot be forced without an allocator hook,\n  still create the test function and document inside it why it cannot be triggered, and\n  instead assert the closest reachable observable behaviour — say which in your report).\n- PROPERTY-STYLE: loop over MANY randomized frames per test (fixed seed, e.g. `Rng::new(N)`),\n  varying payload size, `Shape`, blockSizeID, blockMode, checksum flags, contentSize and\n  compression level. Keep the whole file under ~400s.\n- Cover explicitly:\n  * Whole frame in one `LZ4F_decompress` call with a large dst.\n  * Source fed ONE BYTE AT A TIME (exercises every `dstage_store*` buffering stage) and in\n    randomized small chunks; also dst fed in small pieces so `dstage_flushOut` splits over\n    several calls. Compare the hint returned at every single step.\n  * dst capacity smaller than maxBlockSize (tmpOut path) and much larger.\n  * blockLinked frames large enough to exercise the `LZ4F_updateDict` branches (>64 KB of\n    history, several blocks, dst continuation vs dst switch vs tmpOut-resident dict).\n  * blockIndependent frames at each blockSizeID.\n  * `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t` stableDst 0 and 1 on a blockLinked frame; skipChecksums 0\n    and 1 on a frame carrying BOTH content and block checksums (also verify skipChecksums=1\n    makes an otherwise-invalid checksum decode successfully in both libraries).\n  * Stored/uncompressed blocks (incompressible payload → `dstage_copyDirect`), including a\n    copy split across calls and a following block checksum.\n  * Two frames concatenated into one dctx; a frame followed by a skippable frame; srcSize=0\n    (expect the minFHSize hint); a hint-only call with dstBuffer NULL and `*dstSizePtr`=0.\n  * Skippable frames: all 16 magic values `0x184D2A50..=0x184D2A5F`, content size 0, small,\n    and larger than the supplied input (split across calls), plus the 8-byte header split\n    across calls.\n  * `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict`: dict supplied before init (applied), supplied mid-frame\n    (ignored), dictSize 0, < 64 KB, == 64 KB, > 64 KB; and a frame that was compressed with\n    the matching dict via `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict` so the dict is actually needed.\n  * ERROR rows: bad magic → `err(13)`; FLG bit1 set → `err(8)`; FLG version != 1 → `err(6)`;\n    BD bit7 set → `err(8)`; BD low nibble non-zero → `err(8)`; blockSizeID 0..3 → `err(2)`;\n    wrong header checksum byte → `err(17)`; truncated header (srcSize 0..6) → `err(12)`;\n    declared block size > frame maxBlockSize → `err(2)`; blockHeader == 0 → clean end of\n    frame; truncated compressed block / corrupt block payload → `err(16)`; corrupted block\n    checksum on a COMPRESSED block and on a STORED block → `err(7)`; corrupted content\n    checksum → `err(18)`; contentSize declared but decoded total smaller → `err(14)`;\n    `LZ4F_headerSize` NULL src → `err(15)` and srcSize<5 → `err(12)`;\n    `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` mid-header → `err(19)`; `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext(NULL, ..)`\n    → `err(21)`; `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext` returning the raw `dStage` for a fresh,\n    a mid