STS ONLY. If you find a behavioural\n  divergence between C and Rust, leave the test in place (failing) and REPORT it precisely:\n  function, exact inputs, C result, Rust result.\n- Never call Rust functions directly — every call goes through a `.so` symbol via libloading.\n- CRITICAL: opaque contexts (`LZ4F_cctx`, `LZ4F_dctx`) must be created by EACH library for\n  ITSELF and freed by the same library. NEVER hand a context from one library to the other.\n- Cargo has NO network access. ALWAYS pass `--offline`:\n  `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test lz4frame_decomp 2>&1 | tail -40`\n\nHARNESS (already written; READ IT: `translation/tests/common/mod.rs`; also look at the\nexisting `translation/tests/lz4file.rs` for a working example of driving the lz4frame API)\nStart with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::os::raw::{c_char, c_int, c_uint, c_void};\n```\n`libs()` -> `&'static Pair`; `l.sym::<FnType>(\"name\")` -> `(c_fn, rust_fn)`.\nHelpers: `Rng::new(seed)`, `gen(&mut rng, Shape::X, len)`, `ALL_SHAPES`,\n`interesting_sizes()`, `same_usize_and_bytes`, `same_full_buffers`, `first_diff`, `hexdump`,\n`err(code)` = `(size_t)-code`, `is_err_range(r)`, plus the `#[repr(C)]` mirrors\n`LZ4F_frameInfo_t`, `LZ4F_preferences_t`, `LZ4F_compressOptions_t`,\n`LZ4F_decompressOptions_t` and the `LZ4F_*` constants. Add local\n`type Fn... = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(...)` aliases as needed.\n\nKEY TECHNIQUE\nBuild reference frames with the C library's `LZ4F_compressFrame` (or the low-level pipeline)\nso both decoders receive EXACTLY the same input bytes. For the malformed cases, hand-craft\nor surgically corrupt the frame bytes. For every `LZ4F_decompress` call, C and Rust get\ntheir OWN dst buffers (0xCD-filled, with a guard tail) and their own `dstSize`/`srcSize`\nin/out variables — compare the return value (the \"hint\"), BOTH out-params\n(`*dstSizePtr`, `*srcSizePtr`) and the produced bytes after EVERY call.\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n- One `#[test] fn row_NNN_...()` per CONFIGS row 142..156 (every number must appear in a\n  test function name) plus `#[test] fn err_NN_...()` tests for ERRORS.md rows 24..55 (every\n  number 24..=55 must appear in some test function name; for the rows that ERRORS.md marks\n  as UNREACHABLE or as allocation failures that cannot be forced without an allocator hook,\n  still create the test function and document inside it why it cannot be triggered, and\n  instead assert the closest reachable observable behaviour — say which in your report).\n- PROPERTY-STYLE: loop over MANY randomized frames per test (fixed seed, e.g. `Rng::new(N)`),\n  varying payload size, `Shape`, blockSizeID, blockMode, checksum flags, contentSize and\n  compression level. Keep the whole file under ~400s.\n- Cover explicitly:\n  * Whole frame in one `LZ4F_decompress` call with a large dst.\n  * Source fed ONE BYTE AT A TIME (exercises every `dstage_store*` buffering stage) and in\n    randomized small chunks; also dst fed in small pieces so `dstage_flushOut` splits over\n    several calls. Compare the hint returned at every single step.\n  * dst capacity smaller than maxBlockSize (tmpOut path) and much larger.\n  * blockLinked frames large enough to exercise the `LZ4F_updateDict` branches (>64 KB of\n    history, several blocks, dst continuation vs dst switch vs tmpOut-resident dict).\n  * blockIndependent frames at each blockSizeID.\n  * `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t` stableDst 0 and 1 on a blockLinked frame; skipChecksums 0\n    and 1 on a frame carrying BOTH content and block checksums (also verify skipChecksums=1\n    makes an otherwise-invalid checksum decode successfully in both libraries).\n  * Stored/uncompressed blocks (incompressible payload → `dstage_copyDirect`), including a\n    copy split across calls and a following block checksum.\n  * Two frames concatenated into one dctx; a frame followed by a skippable frame; srcSize=0\n    (expect the minFHSize hint); a hint-only call with dstBuffer NULL and `*dstSizePtr`=0.\n  * Skippable frames: all 16 magic values `0x184D2A50..=0x184D2A5F`, content size 0, small,\n    and larger than the supplied input (split across calls), plus the 8-byte header split\n    across calls.\n  * `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict`: dict supplied before init (applied), supplied mid-frame\n    (ignored), dictSize 0, < 64 KB, == 64 KB, > 64 KB; and a frame that was compressed with\n    the matching dict via `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict` so the dict is actually needed.\n  * ERROR rows: bad magic → `err(13)`; FLG bit1 set → `err(8)`; FLG version != 1 → `err(6)`;\n    BD bit7 set → `err(8)`; BD low nibble non-zero → `err(8)`; blockSizeID 0..3 → `err(2)`;\n    wrong header checksum byte → `err(17)`; truncated header (srcSize 0..6) → `err(12)`;\n    declared block size > frame maxBlockSize → `err(2)`; blockHeader == 0 → clean end of\n    frame; truncated compressed block / corrupt block payload → `err(16)`; corrupted block\n    checksum on a COMPRESSED block and on a STORED block → `err(7)`; corrupted content\n    checksum → `err(18)`; contentSize declared but decoded total smaller → `err(14)`;\n    `LZ4F_headerSize` NULL src → `err(15)` and srcSize<5 → `err(12)`;\n    `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` mid-header → `err(19)`; `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext(NULL, ..)`\n    → `err(21)`; `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext` returning the raw `dStage` for a fresh,\n    a mid-frame and a completed context (assert the exact value).\n    Assert the EXACT error code from both libraries, never merely \"both failed\".\n  * After each error, keep using the SAME dctx (and after `LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext`)\n    and keep comparing — error-state recovery must match too.\n- FUZZ: generate valid frames, then apply randomized single-byte flips / truncations /\n  splices, feed the identical bytes to both decoders (looping until each terminates), and\n  assert C and Rust produce the identical sequence of return values, out-params and output\n  bytes. Do many thousands of iterations across several frame configurations. Report the\n  distribution of distinct outcomes you observed so the fuzzing is demonstrably non-vacuous.\n\nIterate: run with `--offline --release`; fix YOUR TEST when the test itself is at fault (the\nC is always right). Only genuine C-vs-Rust behavioural differences should remain failing.\n\nFinish by reporting: test count, pass/fail counts, runtime, the fuzz outcome distribution,\nand a precise list of any genuine C-vs-Rust divergences.","agentId":"a746603a63964ce11","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"1aaf592dc1a0e3fa","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. One new file written: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iXd6IA/translation/tests/lz4frame_decomp.rs` (4259 lines). Nothing else was touched — `c_src/` and `translation/src/` are untouched.\n\n## Result\n\n**49 tests, 49 pass, 0 fail. Runtime 32.7 s (`--release`, parallel; 45 s single-threaded)** — well under the 400 s budget.\n\nCommand: `cd translation && cargo test --offline --release --test lz4frame_decomp`\n\n### Coverage\n- **CONFIGS rows 142–156**: one `row_NNN_*` test each (all 15 numbers present).\n- **ERRORS rows 24–55**: one `err_NN_*` test each (all 32 numbers present).\n- Plus `fuzz_mutated_frames_are_decoded_identically` and `fuzz_random_byte_streams_and_dictionaries`.\n\nHarness: a `Plan`/`Trace` driver where both libraries get an identical, hint-independent call schedule (cycled src window sizes, cycled dst capacities, `Contig` vs fresh-per-call dst buffers, `max_calls`, `continue_frames`, dict-from-call-N). Every call's **hint, `*dstSizePtr`, `*srcSizePtr`** are recorded and compared step-by-step; the whole 0xCD-filled dst buffer plus a 64-byte guard tail is compared, and `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext`'s raw `dStage` return is compared too. Each library creates/frees its own `LZ4F_dctx`/`LZ4F_cctx`; reference frames come from the C library only.\n\n### Notable findings (all agreements, no divergences)\n1. **`skipChecksums=1` does NOT skip a *compressed* block's trailing CRC.** `lz4frame.c:1878` is not guarded by `dctx->skipChecksum` (unlike `dstage_getBlockChecksum` at :1825 and the content checksum at :2021). My first draft asserted otherwise and failed; the C behaviour is `err(7)` regardless, and Rust matches. Pinned explicitly in `row_148` and `err_45`.\n2. **ERRORS rows 41/42 (allocation failures) ARE forcible** — via the exported `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext_advanced` + `LZ4F_CustomMem` hook. A counting allocator that fails allocation #2 (`tmpIn`) or #3 (`tmpOutBuffer`) yields `err(9)` with `*srcSizePtr = *dstSizePtr = 0`; a retry (allocator now succeeding, resuming at `hsize` since the header was consumed internally but reported as 0 consumed) recovers identically in both libraries. So they are real tests, not documented-as-unreachable stubs.\n3. **ERRORS row 55 tested for real**: a 1 GiB + 1 byte dictionary buffer whose last 64 KB is the dictionary the frame was actually compressed with (`LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict`), on both the decode-into-dst and decode-into-tmpOut truncation sites, plus an exactly-1 GiB control.\n4. **Two genuinely unreachable rows**, documented in-code with the reason and replaced by the closest reachable assertion:\n   - **row 24** (`LZ4F_decodeHeader`, `srcSize < 7`, :1354) — no public path reaches it; asserted instead that `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` with 0–6 bytes gives `err(12)` from :1450/:1507, and `LZ4F_decompress` with 1–6 header bytes returns exactly `(7-n)+4` as a hint, never an error.\n   - **row 51** (`ctxTypeID_to_size` default `return 0`, :676) — `ctxTypeID` is only ever literal 1 or 2; asserted instead that a single reused `LZ4F_cctx` crossing `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN` in both directions (forcing the ctx-type switch + realloc) produces frames both decoders handle identically.\n5. Test-side gotchas I fixed (C is right): `LZ4F_optimalBSID` downgrades the stored BD byte for small inputs (a 5000-byte payload at `max256KB` reports `blockSizeID == 4`), and the 19-byte header requires a non-zero `dictID`.\n\n### Fuzz distributions (demonstrably non-vacuous)\nStage A — 60 000 mutated valid frames (byte flips/replacements, truncations, run deletions, random insertions, cross-frame splices) over 8 base configs:\n```\nerr(7) 16795  err(16) 6250  err(13) 1635  err(2) 1314  err(17) 336\nerr(18) 249   err(8) 268    err(6) 83\nincomplete 27782   ok/original 3374   ok/other 1914\n(59975 mutations changed bytes; 25 no-ops)\n```\nStage B — 30 000 semi-structured random streams, half with a random dictionary via `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict` (sizes 0, 1, 4 K, 65535, 65536, 65537, 300 K):\n```\nLZ4F_decompress : err(13) 15063  err(8) 2225  err(17) 1876  err(6) 1332\n                  err(2) 644  err(7) 251  err(14) 141  err(16) 135  err(18) 118\n                  incomplete 8086  ok/empty 127  ok/data 2\nLZ4F_headerSize : err(13) 14069  size 8 7152  err(12) 1761  size 11 1773\n                  size 15 1766  size 19 1742  size 7 1737\nLZ4F_getFrameInfo: err(13) 14069  hint 4 8475  err(12) 2681  err(8) 1934\n                  err(17) 1607  err(6) 1131  err(2) 103\n```\nNine distinct `LZ4F_errorCodes` observed across the two stages (2, 6, 7, 8, 12, 13, 14, 16, 17, 18).\n\n### C-vs-Rust divergences\n**None.** Every hint, `*srcSizePtr`, `*dstSizePtr`, output byte, guard tail, `LZ4F_frameInfo_t`, and `dStage`-from-`free` matched across ~90 000 fuzz iterations and every targeted case. No failing tests were left in place."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":2581370,"totalTokens":262285,"totalToolUseCount":66,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":497,"cache_read_input_tokens":259589,"output_tokens":2197,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":497},"inference_geo":"","itera