y on the intended loop path; rows 100/102 needing `dstCapacity ≤ 31` to keep the shortcut disabled and `≥ ll+MFLIMIT` to reach `safe_match_copy`; row 99's `ll ≥ 15` header length; row 110's \"legal\" block violating `MFLIMIT`; row 111's third corrupt block being rescued by the stream prefix."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a43ae70eceb30ab95 (use SendMessage with to: 'a43ae70eceb30ab95', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 336305\ntool_uses: 97\nduration_ms: 2930859</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62","uuid":"95b212e5-3996-44a1-abbd-81c7e1c56d26","timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:07:50.894Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iXd6IA\n\nTASK: write ONE new file `translation/tests/errors_block.rs` containing error-path\ndifferential tests for rows 56-159 of `translation/ERRORS.md` — i.e. the whole\n\"## lz4.c (block API)\" section (rows 56-116) and the whole \"## lz4hc.c (HC block API)\"\nsection (rows 117-159). Read those rows first, plus `c_src/src/lz4.c`, `c_src/src/lz4hc.c`,\n`c_src/include/lz4.h` and `c_src/include/lz4hc.h`.\n\nHARD RULES\n- NEVER modify anything in `c_src/`.\n- Do NOT modify `translation/src/*.rs`. You write TESTS ONLY. Report any genuine C-vs-Rust\n  divergence precisely (function, exact inputs, C result, Rust result), leaving it failing.\n- Never call Rust functions directly — every call goes through a `.so` symbol via libloading.\n- CRITICAL: opaque state (`LZ4_stream_t`, `LZ4_streamHC_t`, `LZ4_streamDecode_t`) must be\n  created/initialised by EACH library for ITSELF (its own `LZ4_createStream*` or its own\n  `LZ4_sizeofState*()`-sized buffer + its own `LZ4_initStream*`) and freed by the same\n  library. NEVER hand a context from one library to the other.\n- IMPORTANT: the C reference `.so` is compiled WITHOUT `NDEBUG`, so its `assert()`s are LIVE\n  and will abort the test process, while the Rust has no equivalent. ERRORS.md flags several\n  rows as \"assert-only contracts\" / UB-in-release. For those rows you MUST NOT actually\n  trigger the assert (it would SIGABRT the whole test binary). Instead: keep the test\n  function (so the row is auditably covered), document in a comment that the condition is an\n  assert-only contract that would abort the C library, and assert the closest reachable\n  in-contract behaviour. Say clearly in your report which rows you handled this way.\n  Likewise, do not construct calls that dereference invalid pointers in either library.\n- Cargo has NO network access. ALWAYS pass `--offline`:\n  `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test errors_block 2>&1 | tail -40`\n\nHARNESS (already written; READ IT: `translation/tests/common/mod.rs`. Also read the existing\n`translation/tests/lz4_block.rs`, `lz4_stream.rs` and `lz4hc.rs` for working examples of\ndriving these APIs — reuse their patterns, but do NOT duplicate their happy-path tests.)\nStart with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::os::raw::{c_char, c_int, c_void};\n```\n`libs()` -> `&'static Pair`; `l.sym::<FnType>(\"name\")` -> `(c_fn, rust_fn)`.\nHelpers: `Rng::new(seed)`, `gen(&mut rng, Shape::X, len)`, `ALL_SHAPES`,\n`interesting_sizes()`, `same_int_and_bytes`, `same_full_buffers`, `first_diff`, `hexdump`,\n`LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE`, `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN/DEFAULT/OPT_MIN/MAX`. Signature aliases:\n`FnCompressDefault`, `FnCompressFast`, `FnCompressBound`, `FnDecompressSafe`,\n`FnDecompressSafePartial`, `FnDecompressFast`, `FnCompressDestSize`, `FnVoidToInt`,\n`FnVoidToPtr`, `FnFreePtr`, `FnPtrToInt`. Add local aliases as needed.\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n- One `#[test] fn err_NNN_...()` per ERRORS.md row 56..159; every number 56..=159 must appear\n  in some test function name so coverage is auditable. Several closely-related rows may share\n  one test function as long as every row number appears in a function name.\n- For each row: construct the EXACT invalid input/condition ERRORS.md describes, call BOTH\n  libraries, and assert they return the IDENTICAL value. The lz4 block API has THREE distinct\n  error conventions that must each be checked exactly, never as \"both failed\":\n  * compression returns `0` on failure;\n  * `LZ4_decompress_safe*` returns `-1` OR a negative offset `(int)(-(ip-src))-1` encoding\n    the failure position — assert the exact integer;\n  * `LZ4_resetStreamStateHC` inverts the convention (`1` = failure, `0` = success).\n- PROPERTY-STYLE where there is a value axis: use a fixed seed and MANY randomized inputs\n  (many corrupted blocks, many sizes, many levels) rather than one hand-picked value.\n  Keep the whole file under ~400s (HC level 12 on large inputs is slow — keep those small).\n- Give C and Rust their OWN destination buffers pre-filled with a 0xCD sentinel plus a guard\n  tail, and compare the buffer contents as well as the return value, so a failing call that\n  scribbles differently is caught.\n- Cover, in addition to the enumerated rows, these GENERIC boundary cases (extra clearly\n  named tests):\n  * NULL `src` with srcSize 0, and NULL `dst` with dstCapacity 0, for every entry point that\n    tolerates it (`LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_compress_fast`, `LZ4_compress_HC`,\n    `LZ4_decompress_safe`, `LZ4_compressBound`, `LZ4_sizeofState`, `LZ4_sizeofStateHC`,\n    `LZ4_freeStream(NULL)`, `LZ4_freeStreamHC(NULL)`, `LZ4_freeStreamDecode(NULL)`,\n    `LZ4_freeHC(NULL)`) — assert identical results, and skip (with a comment) any where the\n    C would dereference NULL.\n  * srcSize/dstCapacity of `0`, `-1`, `i32::MIN`, `LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE`,\n    `LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE + 1` and `i32::MAX` passed to `LZ4_compressBound`,\n    `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_compress_fast`, `LZ4_compress_HC`,\n    `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize`, `LZ4_decompress_safe`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial`\n    (use a *lying* oversized length only where the C checks the length BEFORE dereferencing\n    — verify by reading the C; otherwise skip with a comment).\n  * `compressionLevel` and `acceleration` values one step past every documented bound and\n    far beyond: `i32::MIN`, -1000, -1, 0, 1, 2, 9, 10, 12, 13, 100, 65536, 65537, 65538,\n    1000000, `i32::MAX`. The C CLAMPS rather than rejects (ERRORS.md notes\n    `LZ4F_ERROR_compressionLevel_invalid` is dead) — assert C and Rust clamp IDENTICALLY by\n    comparing output bytes, and assert the documented clamping equivalences\n    (e.g. level 0/negative ≡ level 9 for HC; level > 12 ≡ level 12; acceleration < 1 ≡ 1;\n    acceleration > 65537 ≡ 65537).\n  * Undersized and MISALIGNED state buffers passed to `LZ4_initStream`, `LZ4_initStreamHC`,\n    `LZ4_compress_fast_extState`, `LZ4_compress_fast_extState_fastReset`,\n    `LZ4_compress_destSize_extState`, `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC`,\n    `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC_fastReset`, `LZ4_resetStreamState`,\n    `LZ4_resetStreamStateHC`, and the deprecated `*_withState*` wrappers — assert the exact\n    sentinel (`NULL` / `0` / `1` as appropriate) from both.\n  * A large randomized corruption fuzz over `LZ4_decompress_safe`,\n    `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial`, `LZ4_decompress_fast`, `LZ4_uncompress` and\n    `LZ4_uncompress_unknownOutputSize`: many thousands of iterations of byte flips,\n    truncations, zeroed runs (offset-0 matches), oversized length tokens and violated\n    last-literals / last-match rules, asserting the exact returned integer matches between C\n    and Rust every time. Report the distribution of distinct return values observed so the\n    fuzzing is demonstrably non-vacuous.\n\nIterate: run with `--offline --release`; fix YOUR TEST when the test itself is at fault (the\nC is always right). Only genuine C-vs-Rust behavioural differences should remain failing.\nIf a test SIGSEGVs or SIGABRTs, that means you constructed an out-of-contract call — narrow\nit, do not leave the binary crashing.\n\nFinish by reporting: test count, pass/fail counts, runtime, which rows you covered as\nassert-only/unreachable contracts, the fuzz return-value distribution, and a precise list of\nany genuine C-vs-Rust divergences.","agentId":"a43ae70eceb30ab95","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"048a7482be16b10a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. One new file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iXd6IA/translation/tests/errors_block.rs` (6251 lines). Nothing else was touched — `c_src/` and `translation/src/` are unmodified.\n\n## Result\n\n**67 `#[test]` functions, 67 passed / 0 failed, 11.2 s** (`cargo test --offline --release --test errors_block`). Every row number 56…159 appears in some test function name (verified programmatically: 104/104 present, no gaps), plus 5 extra `err_generic_*` tests.\n\n**No genuine C-vs-Rust divergence was found.** Every `same_int_and_bytes` / `same_full_buffers` / exact-sentinel comparison agreed; all 7 initial failures were wrong expectations in my own test (fixed against the C source, listed below).\n\n## Critical build finding that shapes the \"assert-only\" rows\n\n`c_src/src/lz4.c:268-274` defines `assert()` as `((void)0)` unless `LZ4_DEBUG >= 1`, and `lz4hc.c` `#include`s `lz4.c`. The CMake build defines neither `LZ4_DEBUG` nor `NDEBUG`, so **every `assert()` in `lz4.c`/`lz4hc.c` is a no-op** — those rows cannot SIGABRT here. I still treated them as out-of-contract and only exercised the conditions that provably involve no invalid dereference.\n\n## Rows covered as assert-only / unreachable contracts\n\n| Row | Treatment |\n|---|---|\n| 63, 64 | `LZ4_HEAPMODE=0` in CMakeLists → `#if`-excluded. Success side pinned. |\n| 66, 137, 142, 144, 158 | malloc-failure sentinels, unprovokable via the ABI. Success side pinned (incl. that a fresh `LZ4_streamHC_t` defaults to level 9). |\n| 77 | `LZ4_saveDict(_, NULL, n)` would `memmove` to NULL → **not provoked**; tested only where clamping forces `dictSize == 0` (returns 0). |\n| 79 | Exercised for real: `prefixEnd = dictionary + dictSize` is pure pointer arithmetic, no deref. Returns 1. |\n| 88 | `Rvl_t` is 8 bytes → guard compiled out; also `length ≤ 255·srcSize`. Long legal chain pinned instead. |\n| 90, 91, 93, 97, 98, 101 | 64-bit pointer-overflow guards: `length ≤ 255·(2³¹−1) < 2⁴⁰` cannot wrap. Longest legal lengths pinned. |\n| 95 | **Newly identified as dead code**: the fast loop jumps to `safe_match_copy` when `op+length >= oend-64`, which is incompatible with `op+length > oend-5`. Reachable twin is row 103 (tested exactly, `-12`). |\n| 114, 115, 116 | Internal `tableType` contracts; `byPtr` is statically unreachable on 64-bit. Observable consequence (byU16/byU32 pivot at 65547) tested across the boundary. |\n| 124, 126 | Pre-empted by `lz4hc.c:1389`; same observable `0` asserted at lz4mid levels. |\n| 127, 128 | NULL src/dst only with the sizes the asserts permit. **NULL src at level ≥ 10 is skipped**: `mflimit = (BYTE*)0 - 12` wraps, `while (ip <= mflimit)` becomes true and `LZ4HC_FindLongerMatch` dereferences NULL. |\n| 133, 134 | Internal invariants of the match finders; verified indirectly by cross-decoding every HC block with both decoders. |\n| 149 | `select_searchDict_function` is only called under `dict == usingDictCtxHc`, which requires `dictCtx != NULL`. `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary(ws, NULL)` no-op equivalence tested instead. |\n| 151 | Exercised for real at levels 3–12 (no deref). **Skipped at levels 1–2**: `LZ4MID_fillHTable(_, _, (size_t)dictSize)` would read wild. |\n| 156 | Same shape as 77 — only the clamped-to-0 cases. |\n\nAlso skipped with comments (out-of-contract, no sentinel exists): `LZ4_compress_fast_extState_fastReset(NULL,…)` and `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC_fastReset(NULL,…)` (NULL passes `LZ4_isAligned`, then gets dereferenced); undersized buffers for `*_extState*` / `LZ4_resetStreamState*` (the wrappers hard-code `sizeof(...)`, so it's an OOB `MEM_INIT`, not an error); negative `originalSize` to `LZ4_decompress_fast`; lying oversized `compressedSize` to `LZ4_decompress_safe` with positive `dstCapacity`; `LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` as a *lying* srcSize (a legal value that would read 2 GB).\n\n## Fuzz distribution (fixed seed 2024, 400 000 iterations, ~1.13 M decoder calls)\n\n```\nLZ4_decompress_safe:          533 334 calls, 3384 distinct returns in [-1637, 3658]\n                              success=109 408  zero=210  -1=4 648  neg-offsets=419 068 (1100 distinct)\nLZ4_decompress_safe_partial:  400 000 calls, 4244 distinct returns in [-2122, 3651]\n                              success=276 424  zero=4 042  -1=3 315  neg-offsets=116 219 (827 distinct)\nLZ4_decompress_fast:          200 000 calls,  228 distinct returns in [-1, 2502]\n                              success=77 393  -1=122 607\nmutation kinds (8, uniform):  [50248, 50022, 49769, 49870, 49994, 49736, 50282, 50079]\nmost frequent neg offsets:    -2(55952) -3(20831) -5(16434) -7(14064) -11(13385) -6 -8 -9 -12 -10 -13 -4\n```\n`LZ4_uncompress` was cross-checked against `LZ4_decompress_fast` and `LZ4_uncompress_unknownOutputSize` against `LZ4_decompress_safe` on every iteration (identical, both libraries).\n\n## Two behaviours worth flagging (both identical in C and Rust, documented in-file)\n\n1. **Row 104 is not always enforced.** The safe loop's two-stage shortcut (`lz4.c:2228-2255`) copies 16 literal + 18 match bytes and `continue`s without consulting the last-literals rule whenever `ip < iend-16 && op <= oend-32`. A final literal run shorter than `LASTLITERALS` therefore sometimes decodes successfully. Row 104 is pinned exactly (`-12`) with a hand-built block whose literal length is `RUN_MASK` (which disables the shortcut).\n2. **Exact `_output_error` offsets are derived, not observed.** Rows 86/87/89/92/94/99/100/102/103/104 assert hand-derived integers (e.g. row 87 sweep: `-(n-13)`; row 92/100 sweeps: `-(n-2)`; rows 102/103/104: `-12`), plus a truncate-at-the-reported-offset consistency check in `err_105`.\n\nSelf-inflicted expectation bugs found and fixed while iterating (the C was right every time): row 87's off-by-one against `ilimit`; rows 92/100 needing `srcSize ≥ 18`/`≥ 17` to stay on the intended loop path; rows 100/102 needing `dstCapacity ≤ 31` to keep the shortcut disabled and `≥ ll+MFLIMIT` to reach `safe_match_copy`; row 99's `ll ≥ 15` header length; row 110's \"legal\" block violating `MFLIMIT`; row 111's third corrupt block being rescued by the stream prefix."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":2930859,"totalTokens":336305,"totalToolUseCount":97,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":457,"cache_read_input_tokens":333050,"output_tokens":2796,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":457},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":0,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":76,"editFileCount":21,"linesAdded":6441,"linesRemoved":189,"otherToolCount":0}}}
