{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a36aa0ff00c4a6a10","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01P8YuHPhJvDPJmGQytY7hCd","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-glo4ZM/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-iXd6IA/e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62/tasks/a36aa0ff00c4a6a10.output","summary":"All 14 tests written and passing; the whole existing suite still passes (13 binaries, 361 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Deliverable\n\nOne new file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iXd6IA/translation/tests/errors_xxhash.rs` (self-contained: own FFI signature block, `Api32`/`Api64` symbol bundles, `same32`/`same64`/`primed32`/`primed64` helpers copied from `tests/xxhash.rs`). No existing file was touched, nothing in `c_src/` or `translation/src/` was touched.\n\n## The 14 test functions (one per ERRORS.md row 185-198)\n\n| row | test fn | status |\n|---|---|---|\n| 185 | `err_185_xxh32_update_null_input` | pass |\n| 186 | `err_186_xxh64_update_null_input` | pass |\n| 187 | `err_187_update_null_input_accept_null_input_pointer` | pass |\n| 188 | `err_188_oneshot_null_input` | pass |\n| 189 | `err_189_xxh32_createstate_malloc_failure` | pass |\n| 190 | `err_190_xxh64_createstate_malloc_failure` | pass |\n| 191 | `err_191_freestate_null_returns_xxh_ok` | pass |\n| 192 | `err_192_reset_null_state_no_check` | pass |\n| 193 | `err_193_digest_has_no_error_path` | pass |\n| 194 | `err_194_copystate_null_memcpy` | pass |\n| 195 | `err_195_finalize_unreachable_assert` | pass |\n| 196 | `err_196_canonical_static_assert` | pass |\n| 197 | `err_197_lz4frame_ptrdiff_static_assert` | pass |\n| 198 | `err_198_lz4_memory_usage_range_error` | pass |\n\n`14 passed; 0 failed` (`cargo test --offline --release --test errors_xxhash`).\n\n## Forced for real (3 rows)\n\n- **185 / 186** — `LZ4_XXH{32,64}_update(state, NULL, len)` really does return exactly `XXH_ERROR (1)` from both libraries for len 0,1,15,16,17,1000. The NULL test in `XXH32_update_endian` precedes any deref, so this is fully in-contract. Also asserted: digest before == digest after == each library's own one-shot of the prefix (state provably untouched), and that a real `update` afterwards still works and matches `one-shot(prefix||tail)`. Property-style over all 5 `Shape`s × 11 prefix lengths × random seeds.\n- **191** — `LZ4_XXH{32,64}_freeState(NULL)` returns exactly `XXH_OK (0)`, 64 repetitions each, plus the valid-pointer path also returning `0` (so NULL is not distinguishable by return value).\n\n## Covered as unforceable / unreachable / UB (11 rows), with reason\n\n- **187** — verified from `c_src/src/xxhash.c:65-72` that `XXH_ACCEPT_NULL_INPUT_POINTER` defaults to **0** and nothing defines it externally, so the `return XXH_OK` arm is `#if`-ed out of both objects. Asserts the actual configured behaviour: `1` from both `update` entry points, identically, over lengths 0..33 plus 63/64/65/1000/65536/`usize::MAX/2` and randoms.\n- **188** — `len > 0` with NULL is documented UB (the `if (p==NULL)` fixup in `XXH32_endian_align`/`XXH64_endian_align` is compiled out, so `XXH_readLE32(NULL)` faults). **Not invoked.** Only `len == 0` is called (provably no load: `len>=16` false, both residue loops fail immediately with `bEnd==p==NULL`) and asserted equal to each library's own hash of a real zero-length buffer at 8 alignments, over 21 seeds each for 32/64-bit.\n- **189 / 190** — `XXH_malloc` is plain libc `malloc` with a fixed ~48-byte size; no allocator hook exists and interposing a failing malloc would break the harness and the two libraries asymmetrically. Success path pinned instead: 256 simultaneously-live states per library (non-NULL, non-aliasing), each reset→update→digest == the one-shot, plus 2000 create/free churn cycles.\n- **192** — `reset` has no NULL check (the trailing `memcpy(statePtr, &state, ...)` derefs unconditionally). **NULL not passed.** Asserts `reset` returns exactly `XXH_OK (0)` for 70 seeds each side (incl. 0, 1, `0x9E3779B1`, `u32::MAX`, `u64::MAX`, `0x8000…`, randoms), that a reset state digests to `XXH(empty, seed)` in each library, and that reset actually wipes previously absorbed data.\n- **193** — `digest(NULL)` not called; a never-`reset` `createState` result is **not** digested (uninitialised heap, would legitimately differ). Asserts: freshly-reset digest == empty-input one-shot; reset-but-not-updated digest stable over 7 calls; already-digested-several-times state keeps returning the same hash and, interleaved with random-chunk updates, always equals the one-shot of the consumed prefix. 5 shapes × 6 trials × both widths.\n- **194** — `copyState` is `void` + bare `memcpy`, so NULL is UB with nothing observable to compare. **NULL not passed.** Instead: same-library copies only (C←C, Rust←Rust); copy into a state that already held unrelated data (proves whole-state overwrite); then randomly-chunked **diverging** updates on original and copy with the digest of both checked against `one-shot(head||tail_a)` / `one-shot(head||tail_b)` at every step; plus a 4-deep copy-of-copy chain. Both widths, 5 shapes × 5 trials.\n- **195** — the `assert(0)` past `switch (len & 15)` / `switch (len & 31)` is arithmetically unreachable (every residue has a `return`). Asserts every `len & 15` residue 0..=15 and every `len & 31` residue 0..=31 over 6 base lengths (0/1/2/3/8/64 stripes) × 5 shapes × 5 seeds, one-shot, **and** the same residues reached through the streaming API one byte at a time so `finalize` walks the internal `mem32`/`mem64` buffer instead of caller memory.\n- **196** — `XXH_STATIC_ASSERT` is a `1/(int)(!!(c))` enum initializer, i.e. a translation error; both `.so`s loaded so it held. Asserts the protected runtime invariant: canonical written into a `16 + N + 16` sentinel-filled buffer touches **exactly** 4 / 8 bytes (both sentinel regions verified `0x5A`), bytes are big-endian, bytes byte-identical C vs Rust, `hashFromCanonical` round-trips, and also agrees on arbitrary non-canonical bytes. ~607 values per width incl. 0 and all-ones, plus real digests of actual inputs.\n- **197** — `LZ4F_STATIC_ASSERT(sizeof(ptrdiff_t) >= sizeof(size_t))` is compile-time (LP64: 8 >= 8). Asserts the runtime invariant over 0, 1, 23, 24, 25, `err(0)`..`err(25)`, `err(100)`, `err(26/27/50/1000/100000)`, `usize::MAX/2`, `usize::MAX` and 200 randoms: `LZ4F_isError` matches `code > err(24)` (`LZ4F_ERROR_maxCode == 24`) and matches C; `LZ4F_getErrorCode` equals `-(ptrdiff_t)code` and round-trips back to `code`; `LZ4F_getErrorName` compared by **`CStr` contents** against the 25-entry name table from `lz4frame.h` and `\"Unspecified error code\"`. Plus an explicit spot-check table for the exact values the row names.\n- **198** — `LZ4_MEMORY_USAGE` bounds are `#if`/`#error` in `lz4.h:166-172`; a loaded `.so` proves the value was in range. Asserts `LZ4_sizeofState() == (1 << 14) + 32 == 16416` in **both** libraries (and stable across 8 calls), and byte-for-byte agreement of `LZ4_compressBound` + `LZ4_compress_default` at srcSize 65546 / 65547 / 65548 (the `LZ4_64Klimit` byU16→byU32 pivot) for all 5 shapes, including full-destination-buffer comparison and round-tripping each library's block through **both** decompressors.\n\n## Divergences found\n\n**None.** No genuine C-vs-Rust divergence surfaced; all 14 tests pass on the first clean run after fixing my own bugs (three `E0499` double-borrows of `Rng`, and one real self-inflicted `free()` double-free in rows 189/190 where I had written `assert_eq!((c.free)(sc), (r.free)(sr))` followed by a second `(c.free)(sc)` — fixed by capturing the return values once).\n\nTwo notes worth recording for the audit trail: `LZ4F_isError(err(24))` is **false** (the boundary is `code > (size_t)-maxCode`, so `err(24)` itself is not an error and names as `\"Unspecified error code\"`), and `err(1) == usize::MAX` so the prompt's `usize::MAX` case and `err(1)` case are the same value (`\"ERROR_GENERIC\"`). Both are asserted explicitly.","usage":{"total_tokens":119068,"tool_uses":29,"duration_ms":759153},"uuid":"51429ecb-4dff-4719-a6d6-c63de5bf4c9e","session_id":"e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62"}
