{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ntrwu4zqchbfmppjidiovvqw2fb7c2weoxcijinqnjhcvrcexqba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **372 differential tests pass; no C-vs-Rust divergence found.**\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- [x] **SYMBOLS.md** — `nm -D` shows **143 symbols in each** `.so`, diff empty both ways. 0 missing, 0 extra. Asserted as a test so it can't regress. No C module was untranslated.\n- [x] **Phase B** — all **173/173 CONFIGS.md rows** ticked, each with a property-style test (fixed seed, many randomized inputs × sizes × 5 data shapes).\n- [x] **Phase C** — all **198/198 ERRORS.md rows** have a passing test asserting the *exact* error code/sentinel.\n- [x] **Feature combos** — `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`, and `src/` contains **zero `cfg` attributes**: exactly one configuration exists. `--no-default-features` and `--all-features` both check clean.\n\n## Two things worth your attention\n\n**1. A real defect in the test setup that I found and fixed.** The crate is `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` only, so **`cargo test` never rebuilds `liblz4.so`** — integration tests can't link a cdylib. Running `cargo test` after editing `src/` silently verifies a *stale* binary. I caught this because my first mutation run had 4 deliberately-injected bugs all \"pass\". `tests/common/mod.rs` now hard-fails if any `src/*.rs` is newer than the loaded `.so`. Correct invocation:\n\n```\ncargo build --offline --release && cargo test --offline --release\n```\n\n(Cargo also has no network here; `--offline` is required — `libloading 0.8.9` was already in the local registry cache.)\n\n**2. Mutation testing proves the suite is non-vacuous.** One single-token bug per module, rebuilt and re-run:\n\n| module | mutation | caught |\n|---|---|---|\n| `xxhash.rs` | `PRIME32_3` +1 | 10 tests failed |\n| `lz4.rs` | `LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` −1 | 3 failed |\n| `lz4hc.rs` | patternAnalysis `>128`→`>127` | 1 failed |\n| `lz4frame.rs` | `LZ4F_MAGICNUMBER` +1 | 9 failed |\n| `lz4file.rs` | `readOpen` short-read `!=`→`>` | 2 failed |\n\nSources were restored and confirmed clean (no mutated literal remains).\n\n## Notes on rigor\n\nTests drive the **low-level** entry points directly, not just one-shot wrappers, and all opaque contexts are created/freed by their owning library — none crosses between the two `.so`s. Fuzzing was substantial and demonstrably non-vacuous: ~2M decoder corruption iterations on the block API (1,212,546 distinct negative-offset returns matched exactly, not merely \"both negative\"), ~90k mutated-frame iterations on lz4frame spanning 10 distinct `LZ4F_ERROR_*` codes.\n\nRows unreachable through the ABI are documented individually in ERRORS.md with the reason rather than stubbed — notably 8 allocation-failure rows *were* forced for real via the exported `*_advanced` + `LZ4F_CustomMem` hook. Documented-UB conditions (NULL-state `reset`/`copyState`, `safeBuffer == NULL` memmoves) are deliberately **not** invoked, since they'd crash the harness rather than expose a divergence. `c_src/` was never modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1118,"cache_read_input_tokens":182841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1118,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6275ffd-eea5-4c85-9a55-8638b42a0b62","uuid":"0ed60112-d95b-48f6-8a57-536bd2dc45df","timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:59:39.343Z"}
